From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wine.inf: a new user's app and system modes (AppsUseLightTheme 1, SystemUsesLightTheme 0)

Windows writes HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Themes\Personalize AppsUseLightTheme 1 and
SystemUsesLightTheme 0 for a new user. The prefix had neither, and WPF's ThemeMode=System (.NET 9 and
later) takes missing values as dark. Both are now written for a new user, without overwriting a value the
user set (Settings > Colors writes them).
---
diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
index ce8b114..233eac6 100644
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -576,6 +576,10 @@ HKLM,System\CurrentControlSet\Control\Class\{745a17a0-74d3-11d0-b6fe-00a0c90f57d
 [CurrentVersion]
 HKCU,%CurrentVersion%\Explorer\Advanced,,16
 HKCU,%CurrentVersion%\Run,,16
+; the app and system modes as Windows sets them for a new user (apps light, system dark); a program that
+; reads them (WPF's ThemeMode=System) takes a missing value as dark; a user's own choice is kept
+HKCU,%CurrentVersion%\Themes\Personalize,"AppsUseLightTheme",0x10003,1
+HKCU,%CurrentVersion%\Themes\Personalize,"SystemUsesLightTheme",0x10003,0
 HKCU,%CurrentVersionNT%\Winlogon,,16
 HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"CommonFilesDir",,"%16427%"
 HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"FirstInstallDateTime",1,21,81,7c,23
